          "html": "<div class=\"notice subtle\"><h3 class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">已确认的辩题原文</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Confirmed motion wording</span></h3><blockquote class=\"motion-quote\" lang=\"en\">The integration of generative AI tools in the professional development of graduate students not only hinders their critical thinking skills but also their need to be epistemically responsible.</blockquote><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">直译：在研究生专业发展中整合生成式 AI 工具，不仅妨碍其批判性思维技能，也妨碍其在认识上负责任的需要。这里的 <b>need</b> 有歧义，下文保留原词并区分其三种读法。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The wording contains an ambiguity in <b>need</b>. Preserve the original term and distinguish its three interpretations below, rather than quietly replacing it.</span></p> <span class=\"citations\"><a href=\"#src-M00\" aria-label=\"Source M00\">[M00]</a></span></div><div class=\"grid three\"><article class=\"card \"><h3 class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">争议一：作品更好，是否学得更好？</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Clash 1: better output, better learning?</span></h3><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">比较使用 AI 时的完成质量、离开 AI 后的独立判断，以及延迟后的迁移能力。三者可能朝不同方向变化。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Separate assisted output quality, independent judgment after removal, and delayed transfer. They can move in different directions.</span></p></article><article class=\"card \"><h3 class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">争议二：外包哪一部分？</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Clash 2: what is being delegated?</span></h3><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">委托语言润色、生成候选与让 AI 代替判断依据，不具有相同的认知后果。整合方式是核心变量。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Delegating phrasing, generating alternatives and surrendering evidential judgment have different implications. The integration design is a central variable.</span></p></article><article class=\"card \"><h3 class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">争议三：责任还是责任感？</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Clash 3: duty or felt duty?</span></h3><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">觉得不必核验，不代表真的不必核验。风险越大，规范上的核实责任可能越强，实践中却可能履行得更少。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Feeling no need to verify does not remove the duty. A stronger normative need can coexist with weaker enactment.</span></p></article></div><h3 class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">两方最强、也最诚实的路线</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The strongest honest route for each side</span></h3><div class=\"grid two\"><article class=\"card \"><h3 class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">正方：练习与认知责任的替代风险</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Affirmative: substitution risks</span></h3><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">论证整合在现实任务与产出压力下，会把形成理由的练习变成接受现成理由，并削弱承担认识责任的动力与习惯。必须说明这种路径为何具有代表性，而不只是“有人滥用”。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Argue that integration under real task and output pressures can replace practice in forming reasons with acceptance of ready-made reasons, weakening the motivation and habits of epistemic responsibility. Establish why this is representative, not merely possible misuse.</span></p></article><article class=\"card \"><h3 class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">反方：影响取决于设计，责任仍在人</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Negative: design matters; responsibility remains</span></h3><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">承认替代风险，用学习支架、独立核验与真实研究生材料反驳笼统负面结论；指出责任可能转向检验、整合与解释。不能把“可以负责任使用”说成“多数人已经做到了”。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Concede substitution risks; use scaffolding, independent verification and graduate evidence to challenge the broad negative claim. Responsibility may shift toward checking, integration and explanation. Possibility of responsible use does not establish its prevalence.</span></p></article></div><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\"><b>证据综合判断：</b>现有材料足以认真对待特定使用方式的损害，也足以反对把所有整合方式视为同质。它尚未充分建立跨学科研究生长期批判性思维普遍下降的因果结论。双方真正要争的是整合方式、结果指标、外推范围，以及第二分句的含义。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><b>Evidence-weighted assessment:</b> The material supports serious concern about particular uses and rejects treating all integration as homogeneous. It does not adequately establish a general long-term causal decline across graduate disciplines. Contest integration design, outcome measures, transfer and the second conjunct’s meaning.</span></p> <span class=\"citations\"><a href=\"#src-E01\" aria-label=\"Source E01\">[E01]</a> <a href=\"#src-E02\" aria-label=\"Source E02\">[E02]</a> <a href=\"#src-E03\" aria-label=\"Source E03\">[E03]</a> <a href=\"#src-E04\" aria-label=\"Source E04\">[E04]</a> <a href=\"#src-E05\" aria-label=\"Source E05\">[E05]</a></span><p class=\"bi \"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-CN\">本版核对：2026-10-11，Australia/Melbourne。研究是针对辩题的定向综述，不声称穷尽所有研究。证据卡明确区分研究发现与本手册的推论。</span><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Checked on 11 October 2026, Australia/Melbourne. This is a targeted debate review, not an exhaustive systematic review. Evidence cards separate research findings from this pack’s inferences.</span></p>"
